===Development===
{{Quote|People may know Tracer as the poster girl, but she’s not just a character we use on covers and posters; she also encompasses the values of the game, the universe, and the Overwatch development team. The hopeful optimism that she brings, her style, everything about that character was very instrumental to us finding the identity of the game.|[[Arnold Tsang]]}}

====Early Development====
[[File:Jumper.jpg|thumb|The Jumper class]]
Tracer originated from the playable Jumper class from ''[[Project Titan]]''. During the initial pitch for the project that would become ''Overwatch'', the Jumper was invisioned as wielding machine pistols and time bombs, and had the Blink and Recall abilities.<ref>Blizzcon 2017, Overwatch: Archives</ref> From a lore standpoint, multiple Jumpers existed, and were tasked with using their tech to travel back in time to save the world. The Jumper aesthetic was influenced by old aviator jackets and goggles.<ref name = "ForgingWorlds">''[[Forging Worlds: Stories Behind the Art of Blizzard Entertainment]]''</ref>

Most of the concept work on the Jumper was male. This signaled a shift in game design, as while the classes of ''Titan'' were player characters, the characters of ''Overwatch'' were intended to be distinct individuals. The Jumper was thus made female and given a backstory.<ref>''Game Informer #81: Designing Overwatch: From Titan to Torbjörn''</ref>

Tracer conceptually began with the idea of a hero that blinked across the map.<ref>2015-08-08, [http://overwatch.blizzpro.com/2015/08/08/gamescom-livestream-panel-w-the-devs/ GAMESCOM LIVESTREAM PANEL W/ THE DEVS]. ''Blizzpro'', accessed on 2015-08-22</ref> She was the first hero developed for the game;<ref name = "ComicBookTracer">2020-09-18, [https://playoverwatch.com/en-us/news/23524010/comic-book-tracer-cheers-love-the-artist-s-here/ COMIC BOOK TRACER: CHEERS, LOVE! THE ARTIST’S HERE]. ''Blizzard Entertainment'', accessed on 2021-01-23</ref> the first to be made, concepted, modeled, and put in the game.<ref name = "ForgingWorlds"/>

Tracer's visual design allowed the development team to home in on the visual style for ''Overwatch''. The classes from ''Titan'' had a toy-like feel to them, whereas it was decided that for ''Overwatch'', things would be more grounded. This became manifest in Tracer's jacket, as one could see stitching and weathering on the leather. Her legs were shortened during development, as the developers worried it would look too awkward in the game animation.<ref name = "ForgingWorlds"/>

At some point during early development, Tracer shot lasers from her eyes.<ref name = "NewLeadership">2021-04-20, [https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/overwatch/23665015/new-leadership-for-overwatch New Leadership for Overwatch]. ''Blizzard Official Website'', accessed on 2021-04-20</ref> Her design used to include a jacket.<ref name = "Transcript4">2015-05-27, [http://overwatch.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/blizzcon-2014-overwatch-origins-panel-transcript/4 BlizzCon 2014 – Overwatch Origins Panel Transcript]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2015-05-31</ref>

====Character Development====
{{Quote|The question came up of who's the main character in Overwatch? And at first I said, "There is no main character," but I started to think about it differently. Tracer happened to be the first hero we made, concepted, modeled, and put into the game. But the reason why we chose her to be the first is because she is so cool. She embodies so much about the game&mdash;not only in design and aesthetic and color but also in her positive outlook and heroism. It all fit into place.|[[Arnold Tsang]]}}

Tracer is the 'mascot character' of ''Overwatch'',<ref>2015-03-13, [http://overwatch.blizzplanet.com/blog/comments/pax-east-2015-overwatch-hands-on-review PAX East 2015 Overwatch Hands-On Preview]. ''Blizzplanet'', accessed on 2015-03-2015</ref> and its centerpiece hero. She has been called the "[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosetta_Stone Rosetta Stone]" of the game.<ref name = "Transcript4"/> However, her status as the game's "marquee character" was not necessarily planned. During development, the question of who the main character of ''Overwatch'' was came up. At the time, [[Arnold Tsang]] stated that there was no main character, but later reconsidered his stance, as Tracer was the first hero made for the game.<ref name = "ForgingWorlds"/> According to [[Chris Metzen]], Tracer "was one of the first characters we really got to know." While not created for a starring role, the development team warmed up to her. Metzen has likened her to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man Spider-Man].<ref>2015-12-10, [http://www.pcgamer.com/overwatch-story-chris-metzen-interview/#page-2 How Blizzard is making up Overwatch's story as it goes]. ''PC Gamer'', accessed on 2015-12-24</ref> Tsang has stated that Tracer was ultimately chosen to be the main character was because she embodied it with her design, aesthetic, color, and her positive outlook and heroism.<ref name = "ForgingWorlds"/>

After Tracer was given a name and backstory, the game had a clear creative direction; making the shift from classes to heroes.<ref name = "ComicBookTracer"/>

Jeff Kaplan stated that the decision to announce Tracer as a lesbian in the [[Tracer: Reflections|holiday comic]] was considered carefully by the Blizzard team. Kaplan stated that the team wanted to portray Tracer's sexuality in a realistic and non-pandering way that was respectful of the character and tied into her story; not just "checking a checkbox on a list." Kaplan also stated that the team was aware of the negative backlash that the announcement was bound to receive owing to Overwatch's global popularity, that the subject was difficult to talk about, and that it could bring up legal troubles in some countries. Russia banned the comic from appearing on Overwatch's Russian website in accordance with federal law.<ref>2017-4-5, [http://www.polygon.com/2017/4/5/15192058/overwatch-tracer-gay-backlash Making Tracer more than her sexuality was important for the Overwatch team] ''Polygon.com'', accessed on 2017-4-5</ref>

====Overwatch 2====
[[File:Ow2-tracer-concept.jpg|thumb|Overwatch 2 Skin Concept Art by Arnold Tsang]]
Tracer was redesigned for ''[[Overwatch 2]]'' by [[Arnold Tsang]]. The team sought to preserve Tracer's core design elements&mdash;her color palette, silhouette, and sense of motion&mdash;while simultaneously evolving and updating her model and style. This led to a departure from her "retro" goggles, bomber jacket, and leggings and a move toward a sleeker, more tech-y design that befits a freshly recalled Overwatch agent.<ref>2019-11-05, [https://playoverwatch.com/en-us/news/23189038/revving-up-the-engine-overwatch-2-evolving-the-art-panel-recap REVVING UP THE ENGINE—OVERWATCH 2 “EVOLVING THE ART” PANEL RECAP]. ''Blizzard Entertainment'', accessed on 2020-05-16</ref>

